  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Brazil-UK-WFP Partnership on Social Development: Enhancing Capacities in Social Development Policies and Safety Nets Programmes in Low Income Countries through Triangular and South-South Cooperation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity The Brazil-UK-WFP Partnership on Social Development: Enhancing Capacities in Social Development Policies and Safety Nets Programmes in Low Income Countries through Triangular and South-South Cooperation is a component of Building Brazil&#x2019;s Development Impact in Low Income Countries reported by FCDO with a funding type of 109 - Multilateral organisation and a budget of &#xa3;1,250,901. This project benefits Developing countries, unspecified. It works in the following sector(s): Social Protection, Public sector policy and administrative management.</narrative>
  </description>
